# Reflection of Kiki-Jiki: "Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step." Bot1 activates it during its own end step
# on turn 7, after that turn's end step has begun, so the next end step is the one of Bot2's turn 8: the hasty copy of
# the Goblin Shaman is still there in Bot2's main phase and gone on turn 9. (Made earlier in the turn, it is sacrificed
# at that turn's end step: fable-of-the-mirror-breaker-flips-into-a-kiki-jiki-that-copies-the-goblin-for-a-turn.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Fable of the Mirror-Breaker
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Fable of the Mirror-Breaker.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Choose()
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
[T7 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Reflection of Kiki-Jiki.Activate(Goblin Shaman Token)
Bot1.Pass
[T8 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Shaman Token#2.Keywords = Haste
[T9 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Reflection of Kiki-Jiki; Goblin Shaman Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Shaman Token.Keywords = (absent)
